drm/atomic-helper: clear ignore_damage_clips when duplicating plane state

Backport of the upstream fix ("drm/damage-helper: Clear
ignore_damage_clips ..."), not in rpi-6.12.y at kernel/linux.commit.

virtio-gpu (and vmwgfx) set drm_plane_state.ignore_damage_clips in their
atomic_check when a commit brings a different framebuffer, so that the
whole new buffer is uploaded. __drm_atomic_helper_plane_duplicate_state()
memcpy()s the current state into the new one and never clears the flag,
so once the framebuffer has changed a single time - fbcon's to the
compositor's, at the first frame of a session - every later commit
carries it too, and virtio-gpu ignores FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS for good: each
pointer movement becomes a RESOURCE_FLUSH (and TRANSFER_TO_HOST) of the
whole 1920x1080 plane. Seen in QEMU with the trace event
virtio_gpu_cmd_res_flush; this is the pointer lag under UTM.

The flag is meant per commit, like fb_damage_clips beside it, which is
already cleared here.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.c
@@ -367,6 +367,7 @@
 	state->commit = NULL;
 	state->fb_damage_clips = NULL;
 	state->color_mgmt_changed = false;
+	state->ignore_damage_clips = false;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(__drm_atomic_helper_plane_duplicate_state);
 
